<PageLayout title="Cookie policy" heading="Cookie policy" description="My Dutch Door does not use tracking cookies.">
  <p class="note">Draft text. Pending review by a lawyer (see VERIFY.md).</p>
  <h2>No tracking cookies</h2>
  <p>This site does not set advertising or tracking cookies, so there is no cookie banner. We measure visits with a cookieless analytics tool that does not store anything on your device and does not follow you around the web. <span class="verify">VERIFY: confirm the analytics tool and its settings before launch</span></p>
  <h2>What your browser stores</h2>
  <p>After you send a request, your browser keeps a short note (your first name, a masked email address and a one-time code) in session storage, only so the next page can greet you and link the optional questions to your request. It disappears when you close the tab or finish step 2.</p>
</PageLayout>
